# WRYM NOTICE

This file records provenance and attribution boundaries for the WRYM
benchmark. It complements the LICENSE (code, MIT) and LICENSE-DATA
(level & run data, CC BY 4.0).

## 1. Relationship to the game WOIM

WRYM is an **independent, clean-room research benchmark inspired by the
design space of the puzzle game WOIM** (by its respective author/publisher,
available on Steam).

- **No WOIM assets are included or redistributed** — no artwork, sprites,
  audio, level layouts, executables, or other copyrighted material from
  WOIM appears in this repository.
- **No WOIM source code was used.** The WRYM engine (`src/lib/wyrm/`)
  is an original TypeScript implementation of a deterministic worm puzzle
  with publicly-describable genre mechanics (grid movement, apples, crates,
  buttons, gates, spikes, one-way valves, crumble bridges, ice, eggs).
  Game *rules and mechanics* are not copyrightable expression; this
  repository's *expression* — code, art, levels, text — is entirely
  original.
- All 38+ ladder levels, the visual design of the site, the pixel art in
  `site/assets/wyrm-render.js`, and all written material are original works
  of this project's contributors.
- "WOIM IN LOVE!" and similar in-game flavor text used in WRYM run events
  are WRYM's own homage strings, chosen as commentary/reference to the
  genre, not copies of WOIM's asset text.

This is the same boundary drawn by comparable benchmarks built around
commercial games — e.g. Baba Is Harbor: "Apache 2.0 for the code in this
repository. Baba Is You is © Arvi 'Hempuli' Teikari; no game content or
engine code is included or redistributed."

If you are the rights holder for WOIM and believe anything here crosses a
line, open an issue and it will be addressed immediately.

## 2. Model results & trademarks

Model names, Elo ratings, and run archives reference their respective
providers and are measurements produced by this project's methodology.
All model marks belong to their owners; leaderboard rows link to
Artificial Analysis model pages for independent verification.

